  "brief-triage.md": "# gta brief 0007 \u2014 review `borrow.book/s02#component-01` (triage)\n\n- Agent: `gta-reviewer` (read-only)\n- Test class: `com.example.lending.borrow.BorrowControllerIT`\n- Oracle source: `confirmed`\n\n## Scenario `borrow.book/s02`\n\n- **WHEN** inventory-service cannot be reached and client `c-1` books a borrow of `10000` shares of `ACME`\n- **THEN** the response status is `503` and the borrow status is `PENDING_LOCATE`\n\n## What to judge\n\nThe test failed with `TEST_ASSERTION_FAILED`:\n\n```\norg.opentest4j.AssertionFailedError: [HTTP status code] \nexpected: 503\n but was: 201\n```\n\nDecide whether the test, the spec or the product is wrong. Never recommend changing the expected value to the actual value.\n\n## Skills to read first\n\n- `.gta/skills/gta-reviewing-test-quality/SKILL.md`\n- `.gta/skills/gta-designing-test-oracles/SKILL.md`\n\n## Allowed verdicts\n\n- `test-defect` \u2014 the test is wrong (setup, input, mechanics); the locked expected values stay\n- `flaky` \u2014 nondeterministic; only waiting/synchronisation may change\n- `product-defect` \u2014 the code violates a confirmed/documented expectation (a human will confirm)\n- `spec-error` \u2014 the expectation itself is wrong\n- `spec-gap` \u2014 the spec misses a case needed to judge\n- `oracle-defect` \u2014 the locked assertion is mis-written (a human must unlock)\n- `environment` \u2014 fails only because of the local environment\n- `expected-change` \u2014 behaviour changed on purpose\n\n## Return\n\nReply with exactly one line: `verdict: <verdict> \u2014 <one-sentence reason>`. The orchestrator passes it to `./gtaw submit --review borrow.book/s02#component-01 --token s20261116144220-9uib:0007 --verdict <verdict> --reason \"\u2026\"`.\n",
